thatnealpatel/dotfiles2 provides my bespoke,
opinionated setup scripts for things i like.

trust me bro:

```
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thatnealpatel/dotfiles2/main/.bootstrap/bootstrap.sh | bash
exec zsh
```

this script clones this bare repo into
~/.dotfiles and sets up the worktree.
it then executes each of the stages:

flags (after `bash -s --` when piped from curl):
  -ts_authkey KEY  join the tailnet; also read from $TS_AUTHKEY
  -migrate         move a previous setup aside without asking

on a host with a previous setup (oh-my-zsh, an old
~/.dotfiles, ~/sdk, a stale ~/bin/nvim) bootstrap
lists what it found and asks y/N. y moves it all to
~/.dotfiles-backup/<timestamp>/ and installs fresh.

stages (.bootstrap/stages):
  05-tailscale apt repo and package; joins only with a key
  10-zsh       plugins, zoxide, login shell
  20-tmux      tmux-resurrect
  30-go        pinned release as bootstrap, tip built at ~/w/go
  40-go-tools  go install from go-tools.txt
  50-neovim    pinned release built from source

daily:
  d2sync [stage...]                fast-forward $HOME to origin/main,
                                   then re-run the named stages
  ~/.bootstrap/bootstrap.sh 50-neovim   re-run one stage
  .bootstrap/versions.sh           bump a pin, re-run its stage
  .bootstrap/apt-packages.txt      add a package
  .bootstrap/go-tools.txt          add a go tool
  ~/.config/zsh/local.zsh          host-specific shell, untracked
  ~/.config/nvim/lua/local.lua     host-specific nvim, untracked
  .bootstrap/test/run.sh [-i]      run it all in a container

home layout, always created:
  ~/d   downloads and other large things
  ~/p   personal; all code lives here
  ~/w   work
  ~/t   temporary, survives reboots
  ~/s   security

repo layout:
  .bootstrap/    bootstrap.sh, lib.sh, versions.sh, stages/, test/
  .config/zsh/   one file per purpose; ZDOTDIR
  .config/tmux/  tmux.conf
  .config/nvim/  init.lua, no plugins; PaperColor vendored

anything with a hostname, ip, or secret lives in
local.zsh or local.lua, never here.

workflow: edit in a normal clone (~/p/dotfiles2),
commit, push, then d2sync on each host.
the bare checkout in $HOME is a deploy target,
not a working tree.
